# tools/kitty-text.allow - the findings of tools/check-kitty-text.py that stay.
#
# tools/check-kitty-text.py, run by the build, checks kitty/kitty_text.h (the
# UI texts) and kitty/*.c: a KT_ define used nowhere, two KT_ defines with the
# same text, a text with say/ask/tell/names as a verb, a bare "KiTTY" that is
# not KiTTY++, a string literal handed directly to MessageBox*,
# SetWindowText*, SetDlgItemText*, AppendMenu*, InsertMenu* or a ctrl_*
# control constructor. Every finding needs a line here with a reason, and
# every line here must match a finding, or the build fails.
#
# A text change needs the user's OK on the exact wording first: rows marked
# wording debt are reworded when their code is next changed, not as a sweep.
#
# One line per finding:  category | subject | detail | reason
#   unused    | KT_NAME            | -        | reason
#   duplicate | KT_A = KT_B        | -        | reason
#   word      | KT_NAME            | the word | reason
#   product   | KT_NAME            | KiTTY    | reason
#   hardcoded | kitty/file.c       | Call "literal as written" | reason
# A "|" inside a field is written "\|". Matched by the first three fields,
# never by line number; the same hard-coded text twice in one file with the
# same call needs two lines.

# ---- KT_ defines used nowhere


# ---- KT_ defines with the same text


